WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.055 --> 00:00:06.467
Ezra's eyes went wide as he stared at the hole in the fence.

2
00:00:06.468 --> 00:00:10.748
"You want us to crawl through that hole, Ivy?

3
00:00:10.749 --> 00:00:14.719
But what if the opossums attack us?"

4
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:20.682
Glen laughed. "Opossums are the friendliest forest creatures there are.

5
00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:23.809
Well, unless you wake them up."

6
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.752
Ivy peeked through the hole.

7
00:00:25.753 --> 00:00:31.108
"Guys, this is perfect! We can escape tonight.

8
00:00:31.109 --> 00:00:38.002
Let's meet an hour after the last bugle call."

9
00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:42.472
So that was the plan.

10
00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:46.550
Ivy could hardly wait.

11
00:00:46.551 --> 00:00:51.405
That night she lay in her bunk, listening to all the sounds.

12
00:00:51.406 --> 00:00:54.859
Willow and Clara had finally stopped talking.

13
00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.249
Penelope snored softly.

14
00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:04.354
When it was time, Ivy slipped out of bed.

15
00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:07.311
She slowly opened the screen door.

16
00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:13.873
It squeaked a little but not enough to wake up the others.

17
00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:17.695
Ivy sneaked through the dark night toward the square.

18
00:01:17.696 --> 00:01:22.081
Up ahead, she saw what looked like two shining eyes.

19
00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:27.229
"Psst! Glen? Ezra? Is that you?"

20
00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:32.360
"Ivy! Over here!" Glen said a little too loudly.

21
00:01:32.361 --> 00:01:36.400
The two shining eyes were coming from Ezra's face.

22
00:01:36.401 --> 00:01:40.090
"What are you wearing?" Ivy asked.

23
00:01:40.091 --> 00:01:44.526
"These are my homemade night vision goggles," Ezra said.

24
00:01:44.527 --> 00:01:49.017
"I glued two mini flashlights to my glasses."

25
00:01:49.018 --> 00:01:52.308
"Wow, that's pretty cool," Ivy said.

26
00:01:52.309 --> 00:01:55.485
"I mean, if they actually work."

27
00:01:55.486 --> 00:01:58.686
The kids started down the dark trail.

28
00:01:58.687 --> 00:02:02.906
Ezra crashed into Glen, almost knocking him down.

29
00:02:02.907 --> 00:02:05.756
"Hey, watch it!" Glen yelled.

30
00:02:05.757 --> 00:02:08.316
"Sorry," Ezra said.

31
00:02:08.317 --> 00:02:12.013
A few minutes later, Ezra stepped on Ivy's toes.

32
00:02:12.014 --> 00:02:17.438
"Ouch! Ezra, try not to be so clumsy," Ivy said.

33
00:02:17.439 --> 00:02:21.899
"Sorry! I glued the flashlights in front of my eyes.

34
00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.813
I can't see anything!"

35
00:02:24.814 --> 00:02:32.281
Ivy sighed. "Try pushing the glasses up on your forehead."

36
00:02:32.282 --> 00:02:36.053
They tiptoed through the woods behind boys' cabins.

37
00:02:36.054 --> 00:02:41.509
They could hear someone strumming a ukulele.

38
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.324
"That's Mango," Glen whispered. "He

39
00:02:44.325 --> 00:02:48.168
thinks ukulele music puts us to sleep." "That

40
00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:56.241
horrible noise would give me nightmares," Ivy said. Just

41
00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.843
then Ezra tripped over a rock and made a loud noise. "Who—who's

42
00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:04.123
there?" Mango cried. Ivy

43
00:03:04.124 --> 00:03:07.465
and the boys froze in place. "Hoo,

44
00:03:07.466 --> 00:03:13.193
hoo, hoo, hoo, hoo!" Glen called, imitating an owl. They

45
00:03:13.194 --> 00:03:15.349
heard Mango chuckle. He

46
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:18.909
went back to playing his ukulele. Overhead

47
00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:21.993
the moon was shining. Its

48
00:03:21.994 --> 00:03:24.843
silver light reflected off the lake. A

49
00:03:24.844 --> 00:03:29.219
million stars winked like tiny lights. "I

50
00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:32.185
hope we don't step on a snake." Ezra

51
00:03:32.186 --> 00:03:36.491
moved his head around so the flashlights lit up the path. "Snakes

52
00:03:36.492 --> 00:03:40.688
like sunlight , Ezra," Glen said.

53
00:03:40.689 --> 00:03:45.796
"At night we're more likely to run into skunks. Or wolves."

54
00:03:45.797 --> 00:03:52.080
"W-wolves?" Ezra asked, his voice shaking.

55
00:03:52.081 --> 00:03:58.449
Ivy poked Glen in the ribs with her elbow. "You're not being helpful."

56
00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:01.573
They came to a fork in the path.

57
00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:06.112
Ivy turned right, and Glen turned left.

58
00:04:06.113 --> 00:04:11.964
Ezra stumbled off the path and fell into a bush.

59
00:04:11.965 --> 00:04:15.913
"The hole in the fence is this way," Ivy said.

60
00:04:15.914 --> 00:04:20.419
Glen pointed left. "No, it's this way."

61
00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.895
"I think Ivy's right.

62
00:04:22.896 --> 00:04:29.480
I mean, correct. We go to the right," Ezra said, picking leaves out of his hair.

63
00:04:29.481 --> 00:04:34.152
Glen sighed. "We can't get lost.

64
00:04:34.153 --> 00:04:40.412
Then the amazing Glen Brown escape legend won't be very . . . um, amazing."

65
00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:44.465
They hiked down the trail until Ivy stopped suddenly.

66
00:04:44.466 --> 00:04:48.019
"Look! There's the hole in the fence."

67
00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:50.882
She ducked down and crawled through the opening.

68
00:04:50.883 --> 00:04:53.657
Glen was right behind her.

69
00:04:53.658 --> 00:04:56.131
Ezra put one foot through the hole.

70
00:04:56.132 --> 00:04:59.714
Just then a shrill whistle pierced the night.

71
00:04:59.715 --> 00:05:03.003
A bright light shone right in the kids' eyes.

72
00:05:03.004 --> 00:05:06.070
"Freeze, campers!" a voice shouted.

73
00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:08.930
"Don't take another step!"

